// rule: lex.line-end
// mode: parse
// A line break ends a statement unless the line ends with a binary operator, a comma or an
// opening bracket. A line that starts with `- b` is a new statement. A line that starts with
// something that can't start a statement but continues the one above, such as a binary
// operator other than `-`, `?` or a body's `{`, is an error whose fix joins the lines.
